From b142c956d4bc88903bef426f3d1f2854d90dfe1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 19:13:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arcane backend: Arccore built with SYCL, GPU architectures

- The 'arcane' configuration accepts an Arccore built with SYCL. The
  sources are compiled as C++ (-x c++) by the SYCL compiler that built
  Arccore (TFEL_ARCANE_SYCL_COMPILER: acpp or icpx). The identifier of the
  policy is 'arcane:sycl'. A library compiled in this mode accepts the
  SYCL, Thread and Sequential queues.
- Atomic operations of the statistics: sycl::atomic_ref with SYCL, as in
  the 'sycl' backend. The stack size of the threads is not changed with
  SYCL.
- TFEL_ARCANE_GPU_ARCHITECTURES gives the GPU architectures with CUDA and
  HIP ('native' by default), for a machine without GPU.
- config-arcane.json no longer gives -std: tfel-config gives it, and acpp
  refuses a second one, as in the configurations using acpp.
- Tests: queue of the GPU 'sycl' (default when Arccore is built with
  SYCL). The data of the tests are in the unified memory of Arccore in all
  modes. Its allocators take the size of a block to free it, so
  'deallocate' of the runtime of the tests takes the number of values, as
  std::allocator.
- Documentation of both interfaces.
